.TH I3LOCK-WARPMAN 1 "2026" "warpman" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
i3lock-warpman \- screen locker for i3 / X11 with the warpman drift animation
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B i3lock-warpman
[\fIdrift options\fR] [\fB\-\-\fR \fIcommand\fR]
.br
.B i3lock-warpman \-\-preview
[\fIdrift options\fR]
.br
.B i3lock-warpman \-\-saver
[\fIdrift options\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B i3lock-warpman
locks the screen with
.BR xsecurelock (1)
and runs the warpman drift animation as its saver on every monitor: a thin tinted grid
on black, bent by slowly wandering lenses, rendered with OpenGL straight into the
window xsecurelock creates. It stops drawing while the monitor is off (DPMS).
.PP
When locking it sets XSECURELOCK_SAVER to itself, and XSECURELOCK_SHOW_DATETIME=1 and
XSECURELOCK_SAVER_RESET_ON_AUTH_CLOSE=0 unless they are already set; other
XSECURELOCK_* variables pass through. A \fIcommand\fR after \fB\-\-\fR is passed on to
xsecurelock, which runs it while the screen is locked.
.PP
xsecurelock runs \fBi3lock-warpman\fR again as the saver, with $XSCREENSAVER_WINDOW
set (\fB\-\-saver\fR does the same explicitly). \fB\-\-preview\fR opens the animation in
a normal window.
.SH DRIFT OPTIONS
The same as
.BR swaylock-warpman (1),
plus:
.TP
.BI \-\-window\-id " XID"
Draw into this window (default: $XSCREENSAVER_WINDOW).
.TP
.BI \-W " N" "\fR, \fP" \-H " N"
Size of the preview window (default 1280x800).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
The DRIFT_* variables set the option defaults, as for
.BR swaylock-warpman (1).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/warpman-lock-x11.log
Saver log, started afresh on each lock.
.SH EXAMPLE
In the i3 config:
.PP
.nf
set $lock i3lock-warpman
exec \-\-no\-startup\-id xss\-lock \-\-transfer\-sleep\-lock \-\- $lock
bindsym $mod+BackSpace exec \-\-no\-startup\-id $lock
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR xsecurelock (1),
.BR xss-lock (1),
.BR swaylock-warpman (1)
